{"name":"Dairy Cream","hex":"#edd2a4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dairy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(also dairy products or dairy produce) Products produced from milk.","A place that produces, processes, or sells such products:\nA place, often on a farm, where milk is processed and turned into products such as butter and cheese."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Referring to products produced from milk.\n Referring to products produced from animal milk as opposed to non-milk substitutes.","Referring to products produced from animal milk as opposed to non-milk substitutes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dairy"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dairy","blocks":[{"text":"A dairy farm is a place where milk is stored and where butter, cheese, and other dairy products are made, or a place where those products are sold. It may be a room, a building, or a larger establishment. In the United States, the word may also describe a dairy farm or the part of a mixed farm dedicated to milk for human consumption, whether from cows, buffaloes, goats, yaks, sheep, horses or camels."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Alte_Batzenalpe_2014_Interior_06.jpg/330px-Alte_Batzenalpe_2014_Interior_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dairy"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg/500px-Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg/1280px-Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg/500px-Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Frieze of the Dairy\" showing the façade of the temple of the goddess Ninhursag at Tell al-Ubaid, 2800-2600 BCE, depicting the production of cow dairy products in the stables of the complex, with aman milking on the right and, on the left, men decanting and churning in large containers to obtain cream, butter and cheese, Sumerian Gallery of the Iraq Museum[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-'Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/The_Women%27s_Land_Army_in_Britain%2C_1915-1918_Q30682.jpg/500px-The_Women%27s_Land_Army_in_Britain%2C_1915-1918_Q30682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/The_Women%27s_Land_Army_in_Britain%2C_1915-1918_Q30682.jpg/500px-The_Women%27s_Land_Army_in_Britain%2C_1915-1918_Q30682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A member of the Women's Land Army milking a cow during World War I","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Women's_Land_Army_in_Britain%2C_1915-1918_Q30682.jpg"}